## Question 2: Display Each User's Orders and Average Order Amount

### SQL Query

```sql
SELECT
    user_id,
    order_id,
    order_amount,
    AVG(order_amount) OVER (
        PARTITION BY user_id
    ) AS average_order_amount
FROM Orders
ORDER BY user_id, order_id;
```

### Result Output

| user_id | order_id | order_amount | average_order_amount |
| ------: | -------: | -----------: | -------------------: |
|     101 |        1 |       500.00 |               500.00 |
|     101 |        3 |       300.00 |               500.00 |
|     101 |        8 |       700.00 |               500.00 |
|     102 |        2 |       800.00 |               625.00 |
|     102 |        5 |       450.00 |               625.00 |
|     103 |        4 |      1200.00 |               925.00 |
|     103 |        7 |       650.00 |               925.00 |
|     104 |        6 |       900.00 |               625.00 |
|     104 |        9 |       350.00 |               625.00 |
|     105 |       10 |      1100.00 |              1100.00 |

**Explanation:** `AVG(order_amount) OVER (PARTITION BY user_id)` calculates a separate average for each user while keeping every order in the output.

